				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1477,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Import security types explicitly in Tauri IPC server\n\nUpdate the import statements in `Source/IPC/TauriIPCServer/Server.rs` to use explicit qualified imports for the `PermissionManager`, `SecurityContext`, `SecurityEvent`, and `SecurityEventType` types from the `Security` module.\n\nThis change aligns with the project's Rust formatting and naming conventions by resolving the types directly as `Manager::Struct`, `SecurityContext::Struct`, etc., replacing the previous generic `use` syntax. This improves type clarity and ensures strict adherence to the explicit qualification style used across the IPC layer.\n\nNo functional logic is altered; this is a pure refactoring to enhance code readability and maintain consistency with recent modularization efforts.",
			"SHA": "940aac9ca96b60d5cb0deefbf84cd76bf380cd1c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
